# LdSubmit Error Handling

This rule applies when working with error handling in `LdSubmit` widgets or async operations in Liquid Flutter.

## Error Handling

`LdSubmit` automatically handles exceptions and displays them using `LdExceptionView`. User-facing text is produced when the `LdException` is localized via `LdExceptionLocalizer` (see [LdSubmit best practices](ldsubmit_best_practices.mdc)).

**✅ Recommended: Throw typed exceptions and localize them**

The default localizer handles common exceptions (`SocketException`, `TimeoutException`, `FormatException`) automatically. For custom exceptions that only occur in one place, pass `onException` directly to that `LdSubmit` — no extra widget needed, and the mapping stays local to that instance instead of leaking to sibling widgets:

```dart
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return LdSubmit<User, void>(
    onException: (context, e) {
      final l10n = LiquidLocalizations.of(context);

      if (e.exception is NetworkException) {
        return LdLocalizedException(
          message: l10n.networkError,
          moreInfo: l10n.moreInfo,
          exception: e.exception,
          stackTrace: e.stackTrace,
        );
      }
      if (e.exception is AuthenticationException) {
        return LdLocalizedException(
          message: l10n.errorOccurred,
          moreInfo: l10n.moreInfo,
          canRetry: false,
          exception: e.exception,
          stackTrace: e.stackTrace,
        );
      }
      return null; // falls back to an ancestor LdExceptionLocalizer, then built-in defaults
    },
    config: LdSubmitConfig<User, void>(
      action: (_) async {
        throw const AuthenticationException(); // typed, not localized here
      },
    ),
    child: LdSubmitInlineBuilder<User, void>(),
  );
}
```

For exception types shared across many `LdSubmit`s or a whole feature/app, wrap the shared ancestor with `LdExceptionLocalizer` instead — `LdSubmit.onException` (if set) is tried first and falls back to any ancestor `LdExceptionLocalizer`, then to the built-in defaults.

```dart
LdExceptionLocalizer(
  onException: (context, e) { /* shared mapping */ },
  child: /* subtree with many LdSubmit widgets */,
)
```

Prefer `LdSubmit(onException: ...)` when the mapping is local to a single submit action — it avoids mounting a separate widget and never exposes the mapper to sibling widgets or unrelated descendants the way an ancestor `LdExceptionLocalizer` would.

**❌ Not recommended: Throwing `LdLocalizedException` from actions**

```dart
// Don't do this — use LdExceptionLocalizer instead
throw LdLocalizedException(
  message: 'Network error',
  moreInfo: 'Please check your internet connection',
);
```

Typed exceptions plus a localizer centralize copy, respect locale changes, and keep actions easy to test.
